From eee29b14864ef7270273ce373543fb72894fdeba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maksym Vasylchuk <max@buzztv.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:36:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Document the licensing of this build

The license folder the Android package ships for zvbi contains COPYING.md,
whose first clause reads "License: GPL-2+" -- someone auditing the package
would have to read to the src/* clause further down to see that the library
is LGPL-2+, and would still have no way to know the GPL-2 units were
removed from the build. Record both, and what was lost with them, next to
COPYING.md.
---
 LICENSING-NOTE.md | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSING-NOTE.md

diff --git a/LICENSING-NOTE.md b/LICENSING-NOTE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7537c7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSING-NOTE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Licensing of this build of libzvbi
+
+COPYING.md licenses zvbi as GPL-2+ by default and then states, separately, that
+**all files in `src/*` -- the library itself -- are LGPL-2+**, naming the
+exceptions inside `src/`: `pdc.*` and `packet-830.*` are GPL-2, `ure.*` is MIT,
+`dvb/dmx.h` and `dvb/frontend.h` are LGPL-2.1+, `videodev2k.h` is GPL-2+ or
+BSD-3-Clause, and `strptime.*` is LGPL-2.1+.
+
+This build removes `src/pdc.*` and `src/packet-830.*` from `libzvbi_la_SOURCES`,
+together with the only two references to them from LGPL code (both in
+`src/packet.c`) -- see the patch "Build libzvbi without its GPL-2 translation
+units". The library built here contains no GPL-2 object code, which is what makes
+it usable under LGPL-2+ terms.
+
+Consequently the following are absent from this build:
+
+* `vbi_decode_teletext_8301_cni`, `vbi_decode_teletext_8302_cni`,
+  `vbi_decode_teletext_8301_local_time`, `vbi_decode_teletext_8302_pdc`
+* the `vbi_pil_*` family, `vbi_pty_validity_window` and `_vbi_program_id_dump`
+* the `VBI_EVENT_LOCAL_TIME` and `VBI_EVENT_PROG_ID` events, which packet 8/30
+  used to raise
+
+Teletext page decoding, network identification from packet 8/30 (`parse_bsd`)
+and `vbi_decode_vps_pdc` -- which lives in the LGPL-2+ `src/vps.c` -- are
+unaffected.
+
+This note records what was built. It is not legal advice.
-- 
